{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-airtoxics fixture",
    "description": "The `process-airtoxics` fixture: the run's EXECUTION database -- the snapshot's own tables, cut from the default database for this RunSpec and holding its generators' intermediate tables -- mounted on `onroad/model.esm`. It holds no logic: its `data_sources` are the catalogue under the names the model reads, and its one model, `Fixture`, mounts the domain model as a SUBSYSTEM, binds the run's declared counts, and carries the run's inline tests: assertions on the mounted model's intermediate values (`Onroad.*` / `Nonroad.*`) against this snapshot. A test written inside a `{ref}`'d model does not run (finding F47), so the assertions live here, in the document that supplies the data they are about (esm-spec §6.6; conventions §106). run-tests.sh's fixture stage runs them, then emits the model's `out_*` relation and compares it with the snapshot's MOVESOutput. `runspecs/process-airtoxics.esm` reproduces the same run from the DEFAULT database through the same model, so the pair is a differential test of the execution-database cut: one model, one oracle, two catalogues.\n\nUntil 2026-10-30 this file inlined its own copy of the onroad model (23142 lines, frozen at the commit that last touched it), so the logic every fixture shared was written fourteen times. PLAN.md §7.1, docs/esm-conventions.md §106."
  },
  "models": {
    "Fixture": {
      "subsystems": {
        "Onroad": {
          "ref": "catalogues/onroad-execution-db.esm",
          "url_substitutions": {
            "snapshot": "process-airtoxics"
          },
          "bindings": {
            "n_outputRate": 644
          }
        }
      },
      "variables": {},
      "equations": [],
      "tests": [
        {
          "id": "the_run_scope_comes_from_the_execution_database",
          "description": "Year 2020, August, hour 7, road type 4, county 26161, zone 261610 -- byte for byte `process-crankcase-running`'s scope, and its THC block of MOVESOutput is byte-identical to this one's, so the whole activity half and the whole criteria-pollutant parent are already checked end to end by that fixture. The RunSpec XML says month 7 and hour 6; the execution database says 8 and 7, and it is the authority (docs/process-airtoxics.md 0.1). Three run-level numbers are pinned besides: `GPAFract` is 0, so both fuel-effect blends select their normal arm; the temperature is 59.5 degF and reaches only a quadratic whose coefficients are absent; and the A/C activity quadratic is negative and clamps to 0. (The E10 fuel subtype, 12, that the altTHC path's two lookups key on no longer has a run-level variable and is not asserted.) `specificHumidity` and `molWaterFraction` are NOT read by this fixture and have no variable: pollutant 1 never enters the NOx humidity arm.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
