        {
          "id": "the_six_pollutant_processes_are_one_parent_and_five_species_at_three_chain_depths",
          "description": "The run's whole scope, unpacked from `runspecpollutantprocess` and `runspecchainedto` rather than written down. THIS IS THE FIRST FIXTURE IN THE PORT WHOSE CHAIN IS MORE THAN ONE LEVEL DEEP: 101 (THC) carries a rate of its own; 7901 (NMHC) is chained off it; 8701 (VOC) off 7901; and 2001 (benzene), 2401 (1,3-butadiene) and 2501 (formaldehyde) off 8701. The depths are 0, 3, 3, 3, 1 and 2 in the table's own row order, and every one of the six resolves to the same root, 101, which is why every ratio in this document scales the same THC block. This test pins the six (pollutant, process) pairs and where each rate-row block starts; the chain inputs, roots and depths that it used to assert are gone from the model (the chain is now the `lnk_*` edge list) and are not asserted here.",
          "time_span": {
            "start": 0.0,
            "end": 0.0
          },
          "assertions": [
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_polProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 101.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "variable": "Onroad.rt_polProcessID",
              "time": 0.0,
              "expected": 2001.0,
              "coords": {
                "rate_rows": 165
              }
