          "id": "the_activity_chain_reproduces_the_reference_sho_table",
          "description": "S1-S9, against the four corners of the snapshot's own 82-row `sho` table -- which is byte-identical to `process-tirewear`'s and `process-brakewear`'s, so this is a cross-check between three fixtures as well as against the reference. `activity_rows` is day-major over 41 ages and this run has one day type, so it is 41 rows: row 1 is age 0 and row 41 age 40. It was 82 rows with the weekend block first, which is why every ordinal above 41 moved down by 41 (docs/esm-conventions.md 42).",
